<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 35,600 in Sept.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 35,600 in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in September and average earnings in August. (Previous estimates in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>   UNEMPLOYMENT			SEPT	AUGUST  (AUG PREL)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		  -35,600   -17,300  (-15,600)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			 7.4	 7.5	   (7.5)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change    -72,700    n/a     (+18,376)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate (pct) 7.5	 7.8	   (7.8)</p>
<p>NOTE - Mkts forecast 20,000 September unemployment fall  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)     2.073     2.109     (2.110)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     2.104     2.176     (2.176)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -25,700   -19,200  (-18,600)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -18,900   -17,300  (-17,000)</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS		  AUGUST    JULY   (JULY PREL)</p>
<p>    underlying yearly chng (pct) 4.0	 4.0	  (3.75)</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)		132.3     132.2     (131.8)</p>
<p>    actual yearly chng (pct)     3.6	 4.1	   (3.8)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>    Production-- underlying	4.25	4.0	  (3.75)</p>
<p>		  -- actual	    4.1	 4.2	   (3.8)</p>
<p>    Manufacturing -- underlying  4.5	 4.5	   (4.0)</p>
<p>			-- actual	4.5	 4.4	   (3.9)</p>
<p>    Services -- underlying	 3.75	3.75	 (3.75)</p>
<p>		 -- actual	     3.5	 4.0	   (3.9)</p>
<p>NOTE: Consensus forecast 3.75 pct for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS		  JULY	JUNE    (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago     3.5	 4.1	   (3.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base = 1990)	    113.5     113.3     (113.5)</p>
<p>    3-mth vs same yr/ago	   3.7	 3.8	   (3.7)</p>
<p>    Index (base = 1990)	    113.1     112.8     (113.1)</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OVERTIME HOURS AUGUST    JULY    (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    (million per week)		   8.14	8.35	 (8.58)</p>
<p>    Index (base = 1990)	    99.7	99.9	(101.1)</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING EMPLOYMENT (GB)</p>
<p>    monthly change (April	  UNCH     +19,000   (+13,000)</p>
<p>    Average mthly change last 3m +6,000    +5,000    (+5,000)</p>
<p>    Quarterly change (Q2)	 -16,000    UNCH (Q1)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>(THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>    WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT	Q2	  Q1</p>
<p>    LEVEL				25,819    25,784</p>
<p>    CHANGE			     +35	 -41</p>
<p>    EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT	22,116    22,044</p>
<p>			     CHANGE    +72	 +3</p>
<p>    JOB CENTRE VACANCIES	   SEPT	AUGUST  (PREL AUG)</p>
